  "fanTake": "Drake Maye did what elite quarterbacks do in the clutch—he overcame his own mistakes and delivered when it mattered most, threading that impossible one-handed dime to Efton Chism with 1:50 left to seal a 29-26 road win in Buffalo. Three touchdown passes and a 56% win probability added tells you everything: this wasn't just a victory, it was a masterclass in poise under pressure, especially for a young QB going up against a divisional rival in hostile territory. What makes it even sweeter is how the offense executed in the red zone—four trips, four touchdowns, a perfect 100%—which is the kind of ruthless efficiency that separates good teams from ones that actually win close games. The defense let some opportunities slip (Buffalo converted 50% of their third downs against us, well above the 40% league average), but when the moment came down to inches and seconds, Maye and this offense simply refused to blink. This is the kind of win you build a season on.",
